      "doc_id": "oad_data_dictionary",
      "heading": "ObsAwareData data dictionary > 4. All-sources wide table",
      "text": "`<st>_all_sources_wide.csv` has one row per week, spanning every week in any source (<!-- auto:weeks_all_sources -->2020-08-08 to 2026-10-10<!-- /auto:weeks_all_sources -->), and one column per region, site, measure, and pathogen. Nothing is aggregated or averaged: each ED region and each wastewater site keeps its own columns. Column counts range from about 100 to 3,200 depending on how many regions and sites a state has.\n\n**Column-naming rule:** `[<prefix>]<measure>_<pathogen>[_flag]`. The prefix identifies where the value comes from:"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "oad_data_dictionary#13",
      "doc_id": "oad_data_dictionary",
      "heading": "ObsAwareData data dictionary > 3. Single-source wide tables",
      "text": "`<st>_nhsn_wide.csv`, `<st>_nssp_wide.csv`, and `<st>_nwss_wide.csv` each start with six key columns:\n\n`analysis_region`, `analysis_region_type`, `analysis_region_id`, `raw_geography_type`, `raw_geography_id`, `observation_week`\n\nThese are followed by a pair of columns for every measure and pathogen the source publishes:\n\n| Column name | Holds |\n|---|---|\n| `<measure>_<pathogen>` | the value (`weekly_feature` in the long table) |\n| `<measure>_<pathogen>_flag` | its reliability flag (`observation_state` in the long table) |"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "oad_methods#3",
      "doc_id": "oad_methods",
      "heading": "ObsAwareData methods > 1. Processing overview",
      "text": "   - `<st>_nhsn_wide.csv`, `<st>_nssp_wide.csv`, `<st>_nwss_wide.csv`: one row per region and week.\n   - `<st>_all_sources_wide.csv`: one row per week. The state-level NHSN and NSSP columns, each HSA's NSSP columns, each wastewater site's columns, and the state Census variables are placed side by side.\n   - No values are aggregated, averaged, interpolated, or imputed.\n7. **Join Census context** at the state level only.\n8. **Check and package.** Each state's quality report confirms:\n   - Unique keys\n   - Cell-by-cell agreement between every wide table and the long table\n   - A complete weekly sequence\n   - Agreement between the latest view and the revision history"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "oad_data_dictionary#14",
      "doc_id": "oad_data_dictionary",
      "heading": "ObsAwareData data dictionary > 3. Single-source wide tables",
      "text": "| Column name | Holds |\n|---|---|\n| `<measure>_<pathogen>` | the value (`weekly_feature` in the long table) |\n| `<measure>_<pathogen>_flag` | its reliability flag (`observation_state` in the long table) |\n\nExamples: `hospital_admission_count_covid` and `hospital_admission_count_covid_flag`, `ed_visit_percent_smoothed_rsv`, `wastewater_activity_category_influenza`. The ED `participation_status` has no pathogen dimension, so its columns are `participation_status_not_applicable` and `participation_status_not_applicable_flag`.\n\nRows exist only for (region, week) combinations the source reports. Within a row, a blank value **with** a flag is a reported gap (for example `incidental_missing`). A blank value **and** a blank flag means the source has no record for that pathogen in that region and week."
    },
