      "text": "- **Source**: National Syndromic Surveillance Program:\u202fhttps://www.cdc.gov/nssp/index.html.\n- The acute respiratory illness (ARI) metric categorizes the percentage of emergency department (ED) visits into five activity levels (Very Low, Low, Moderate, High, and Very High), helping people understand the extent of respiratory illness activity in an area. For a list of diagnostic codes for the ARI metric visit: Acute Respiratory Illness Technical Brief."
