      "text": "  - Week 27 through Week 26 of the following calendar year was used to define a surveillance year in order to capture summer COVID-19 activity as the start of a given season.\n  - Lowest activity weeks for ARI were identified as weeks when COVID-19, influenza, and RSV were all identified as having low activity according to their separate thresholds.\n- For each state within a region, the reference periods were used to calculate the values that created the levels (categories) for the 2026-2027 surveillance year."
